# Code Structure Rules

## File Headers (Required on Every File)

JavaScript:
```javascript
/**
 * @file        [filename]
 * @description [What this file does — be specific]
 * @author      Muaishaq
 * @created     [YYYY-MM-DD]
 * @modified    [YYYY-MM-DD]
 */
```

Python:
```python
"""
@file:        [filename]
@description: [What this file does — be specific]
@author:      Muaishaq
@created:     [YYYY-MM-DD]
@modified:    [YYYY-MM-DD]
"""
```

## Function Documentation (Required on Every Function)

JavaScript:
```javascript
/**
 * @description [What this function does]
 * @param       {Type} paramName - [What this parameter is]
 * @returns     {Type} [What is returned]
 * @throws      {Error} [What errors can be thrown]
 */
```

Python:
```python
def function_name(param):
    """
    Description: [What this function does]
    Args:        param (type): [What this parameter is]
    Returns:     type: [What is returned]
    Raises:      ErrorType: [What errors can be raised]
    """
```

## Naming Conventions

- Variables and functions: camelCase
- Classes and React components: PascalCase
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
- Database fields: camelCase
- API endpoints: kebab-case
- File names: kebab-case for JS/TS, snake_case for Python

## File Length

- Maximum 300 lines per file
- If a file exceeds 300 lines, split it into focused modules
